<title>UK: ACPC releases 200,000 bags of coffee to market.</title>
<headline>ACPC releases 200,000 bags of coffee to market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Association of Coffee Producing countries agreed at a technical meeting on Thursday to release an additional 200,000 bags of arabica coffee to the world market in the first half of 1997, ACPC President Rubens Barbosa of Brazil told journalists.  </p>
<p>Barbosa said the technical committee also decided to revoke a previous decision to reduce exports of arabica by 300,000 bags during the same period.</p>
<p>The ACPC decided in January to cut 1.3 million bags of exports -- 1 million bags of robusta and 300,000 bags of arabica.</p>
<p>So the net effect of Thursday's decision will be a reduction of 800,000 bags of exports, Barbosa added.</p>
</text>
